# Blog Migrator - Configuration API Reference

The entire tool is controlled via `src/config.js`. This document explains all configuration options.

## Top-Level Structure

```js
export default {
    BASE_URL: "https://example.com",      // Base URL (informational)
    URLS: [...],                           // Array of URLs to process
    OUTPUT: {...},                         // Output directory settings
    IMAGE_EXTRACTION: {...},               // Image download settings
    DATA: {...},                           // Frontmatter field definitions
}
```

## URLS
Array of full URLs to scrape:
```js
URLS: [
    "https://example.com/blog-post-1/",
    "https://example.com/blog-post-2/",
]
```

## OUTPUT
Directory paths for generated files:
```js
OUTPUT: {
    CONTENT_DIR: "./downloads/content",   // Where .md files are saved
    IMAGES_DIR: "./downloads/images",     // Where images are downloaded
}
```

## IMAGE_EXTRACTION

### Body Image Settings
Body images are automatically extracted from the markdown output - no selector needed!

```js
IMAGE_EXTRACTION: {
    relativePath: "/assets/uploads/",     // Path prefix for rewritten URLs
    filenamePattern: "{slug}-{index}",    // Filename pattern ({slug}, {index} replaced)
    filter: (url) => true,                // Optional: filter function (return false to skip)
    
    featuredImage: {...}                  // Featured image config (see below)
}
```

### Featured Image Settings
Set to `null` to disable featured image extraction.
```js
featuredImage: {
    selector: ".background-inner",        // CSS selector for featured image element
    getValue: (el) => el.style.backgroundImage.replace(/url\(['"]?/, '').replace(/['"]?\)/, ''),
    altSelector: ".heading-text h1",      // Optional: different element for alt text
    getAlt: (el) => el?.textContent?.trim() || '',
    filenamePattern: "{slug}-featured",   // Filename pattern
    frontmatterKey: "image",              // Frontmatter field name for URL
    altFrontmatterKey: "imageAlt"         // Frontmatter field name for alt
}
```

**Fallback behavior**: If featured image selector fails, uses first body image.

## DATA
Defines frontmatter fields. Keys become lowercase field names (underscores removed).

### Static Values
```js
DATA: {
    AUTHOR: "John Smith",                 // Static string value
    CATEGORY: "Blog",
}
```

### Dynamic Values (Selector-based)
```js
DATA: {
    TITLE: {
        selector: "h1",                   // CSS selector
        getValue: (el) => el.textContent.trim(),  // Extract value from element
    },
    DATE: {
        selector: "meta[property='article:published_time']",
        getValue: (el) => el.getAttribute("content"),
    },
}
```

### Special Flags

#### `isContent: true`
Field becomes markdown body instead of frontmatter:
```js
BODY: {
    selector: ".post-body",
    getValue: (el) => el.innerHTML,
    isContent: true,                      // Not in frontmatter, becomes MD content
}
```

## Filename Patterns

### Body Images
Pattern: `filenamePattern: "{slug}-{index}"`
- `{slug}` - URL slug (e.g., "brook-farm-wedding")
- `{index}` - Zero-padded index (01, 02, 03...)

Result: `brook-farm-wedding-01.jpg`, `brook-farm-wedding-02.jpg`

### Featured Image
Pattern: `filenamePattern: "{slug}-featured"`
- `{slug}` - URL slug

Result: `brook-farm-wedding-featured.jpg`

## Image Filter Function

Optional filter to skip certain image URLs:
```js
filter: (url) => {
    // Skip external CDN images
    if (url.includes('getnarrativeapp.com')) return false;
    // Skip placeholder images
    if (url.includes('placeholder')) return false;
    return true;
}
```

## Common Selector Patterns

### WordPress/Uncode Theme
```js
// Featured image from CSS background
selector: ".background-inner"
getValue: (el) => el.style.backgroundImage.replace(/url\(['"]?/, '').replace(/['"]?\)/, '')

// Title
selector: ".heading-text h1"

// Post body
selector: ".post-body"
```

### Standard WordPress
```js
// Featured image
selector: ".wp-post-image"
getValue: (el) => el.src

// Content
selector: ".entry-content"
```
